course: dictionary
lesson: 9785
title: Surroundings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your surroundings are everything around you: the place you are in, and the things and conditions near you. Notice that it is always used in the plural, as «surroundings», because it covers many things at once.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. «Animals are adapted to their surroundings» tells you that animals fit the place where they live. «A goldfish... can turn pale... to match their surroundings» shows that surroundings include the light and colours nearby.
explain: To be aware of your surroundings means to look and listen around you, especially when crossing a road, walking alone or using a phone. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Reptiles get their body heat from everything around them» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Surroundings means everything around you: the place you are in and the things and conditions near you.
fact: «Surroundings» is always used in the plural, even when you mean just one place.
fact: «Camouflage» means looking like your surroundings so that you are hard to notice.
fact: Reptiles are «cold-blooded»: they get their body heat from their surroundings.
fact: Mammals and birds keep warm from inside, but fish, amphibians and reptiles take their warmth from their surroundings.
exercise: What does «surroundings» mean? | The parts of an animal inside its body | Special clothes worn for hide-and-seek | Only the people who live with you | *Everything around you, including the place and conditions near you
exercise: «Camouflage means looking like your surroundings so that hunters do not notice you.» Find and copy the word that means the place and things near you. | camouflage | *surroundings | hunters | notice
exercise: Why are reptiles called cold-blooded? | They are always cold to touch because they dislike warm places | *They get their body heat from their surroundings | They have no blood at all | They live only in icy places
test: In stories, «new surroundings» can make a character nervous or curious. What are new surroundings? | A kind of food that animals eat | A list of rules at school | *A new place and the things around the character | Old clothes that a character wears at home
test: Which phrase means you should look and listen around you when crossing a road? | *be aware of your surroundings | natural surroundings | in new surroundings | camouflage
exam: Ayo says, «Surroundings is only used for one place, so it is singular.» Is Ayo right? | Yes, it means one place only | No, it is used only in science lessons | *No, it is always plural: surroundings | Yes, but only when talking about animals
